# Verify locally before done

Do **not** treat a feature, fix, or refactor as complete until local checks pass. GitHub CI mirrors [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](.github/workflows/ci.yml).

## Required (every code change)

From the repo root, with dependencies installed (`pnpm install`):

```bash
pnpm ci:quality
```

This runs: `pnpm lint` → `pnpm typecheck` → `pnpm test:run` → `pnpm knip`.

Fix failures before finishing. Do not push or ask the user to merge while these fail.

## When routes, SSR, planner UI, or exports change

Also run (needs `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.local`, same as production Neon):

```bash
pnpm build
pnpm test:e2e
```

First-time Playwright on a machine: `pnpm exec playwright install --with-deps chromium`.

CI uses the `DATABASE_URL` GitHub Actions secret for build and e2e; locally use `.env.local`.

## Scope guidance

| Change | Minimum checks |
|--------|----------------|
| Any TS/TSX | `pnpm ci:quality` |
| `src/app/**`, SEO, sitemap, `generateStaticParams` | + `pnpm build` |
| Planner UI / `e2e/**` | + `pnpm test:e2e` |
| Docs-only | Not required unless you edited config |

## Agent behavior

- Run the relevant commands yourself; do not only suggest them.
- If a check cannot run (e.g. missing `DATABASE_URL`), say so and run everything else that can run.
- After fixing CI failures on a branch, re-run the same commands to confirm green.
